U.S. Bank / City of /Cheyenne, WY

Collateral Assignment of Architect's Contract
12187-0018/LEGAL28043180.2
1
COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF ARCHITECT'S CONTRACT

THIS COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF ARCHITECT'S CONTRACT (the
"Assignment") is made as of November 18, 2013 by CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING a
municipal corporation duly organized and existing under the Constitution of the State of Wyoming
("City") to U.S. BANK NATIONAL ASSOCIATION, a national banking association, its
successors and assigns ("Bank").

RECITALS:

A. City has executed a Purchase Agreement of even date (the "PSA") evidencing the
purchase of certain property and improvements that will be improved ("Project") which is located
upon that certain real property more particularly described on Exhibit A, attached hereto and made
a part hereof by this reference ("Land").  Capitalized terms not otherwise defined herein shall have
the meaning given to them in the PSA (as it may be amended, restated, extended, renewed, or
otherwise modified from time to time).

B.
City has entered into a contract with Pappas & Pappas Architects, P.C. ("Architect"),
pertaining to the design and construction of certain improvements to be constructed on the Land in
accordance with the Plans ("Improvements"), and any and all extensions, modifications or renewals
thereof (the "Contract"), a true and correct copy of which is attached hereto as Exhibit B and by
this reference incorporated herein.

C.
The Bank has required City to assign the Contract to Bank and requires Architect to
consent to and accept the assignment as a condition to Bank's purchase of the Project and payment
of the Acquisition Price as described in the PSA, and the Bank would not purchase the Project or
advance the Acquisition Price on the same terms and conditions, without this Assignment and the
consent of the Architect.

ASSIGNMENT

FOR VALUE RECEIVED, the receipt and sufficiency of which is hereby acknowledged,
and as part of the consideration for the purchase of the Project, City and Bank agree as follows:

1.
Assignment.  The City, does hereby assign to the Bank, its participants, successors,
assigns, designees, nominees, or any subsequent owner of the Project, all of City's right, title and
interest in and to the Contract, and any rights, benefit, warranties or remedies arising from any of
the foregoing.
2.
Representations and Warranties of City.  City represents and warrants that:
(a)
The Contract is held by City or when acquired by City will be held by City
free and clear of all liens, security interests and charges and the Contract has not been pledged as
collateral for any obligations other than the assignment contained in this Assignment.  The City
covenants and agrees with Bank to perform all acts required of it to maintain the Contract in good
standing at all times.
```

