6.
Bank's Counsel.  Following a Nonappropriation Event or an Event of Default, the
Bank shall have the right at any time to appear in and defend and be represented by counsel of its
own choice in any action or proceeding purporting to affect City's rights related to the Contract.
7.
Additional Indebtedness/Nonappropriation.  All sums advanced or paid by the Bank
under the terms hereof, all amounts paid, suffered or incurred by the Bank in exercising any
authority granted herein, including reasonable attorneys' fees, and all other amounts due the Bank
from City in connection with this Assignment, the PSA or the Lease shall be added to the
indebtedness evidenced by the PSA and Lease subject to the non-appropriation provisions in the
PSA and Lease, provided however, a Nonappropriation Event shall not terminate this Assignment
but shall entitle Bank to elect to step into the place of City and continue to make payments required
by the Contract so long as Architect performs, or terminate the Contract, as determined by Bank.
8.
City Liability.  Neither the execution and delivery of this Assignment nor any failure
on the part of any person to comply with, honor and perform in accordance with the terms of the
Contract shall affect the liability of any party to pay and perform the obligation under the PSA and
Lease.
9.
No Release.  The taking of this Assignment by the Bank shall not effect the release
of any other collateral now or hereafter held by the Bank as security for the obligations as described
in the PSA or Lease, nor shall the taking of additional security for the obligations described in the
PSA or Lease hereafter effect a release or termination of this Assignment or any terms, conditions
or provisions hereof.
10.
Termination.  Upon payment in full of the Purchase Price and all other sums due if
City exercises its option to purchase the Project described in Article 10 of the Lease, this
Assignment shall cease, terminate and be of no further effect; provided, however, that the affidavit,
certificate, letter or statement of the Bank or any officer, agent or attorney of the Bank showing any
part of the Purchase Price or other amounts payable for the exercise being unpaid shall constitute
conclusive evidence of the validity, effectiveness, and continuing force of this Assignment and any
person may, and is hereby authorized to, rely thereon.  City hereby authorizes and directs all entities
having any interest in the Contract, upon receipt of written notice from the Bank, to recognize the
Bank as entitled to exercise all powers and receive all benefits of City thereunder.
11.
Further Assurances.  City, upon request of the Bank, shall execute and deliver such
additional documents, including but not limited to financing statements, and do such other acts as
