### Page 6 of 8

```text
U.S. Bank / City of /Cheyenne, WY

Collateral Assignment of Architect's Contract
12187-0018/LEGAL28043180.2
6
ARCHITECT'S CONSENT TO COLLATERAL ASSIGNMENT OF
CONTRACT

The undersigned, Pappas & Pappas Architects, P.C. ("Architect"), hereby consents to the
above Assignment as same pertains to the Contract and all amendments, modifications,
supplements, revisions, general conditions and addenda thereto, and as an inducement to the Bank
to make, and in consideration of Bank entering into the PSA and Lease with the City described
hereinabove, agrees as follows:

1. Continued Performance.  Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default by the City
under any instrument, document or agreement relating to the PSA or Lease, the Architect, at the
Bank's request, will continue performance under and in accordance with the Contract, provided that
the Architect shall be reimbursed in accordance with the Contract for all services rendered pursuant
to the Contract.
2. Enforcement of Contract.  After an Event of Default, the Bank may enforce the
Contract in accordance with its terms pursuant to the Assignment and may perform the obligations
of City under the Contract, and Architect will accept such performance in lieu of performance by
City in satisfaction of City's obligations thereunder.
3. No Termination of Contract.  Architect will not terminate the Contract on account of
any default of City thereunder without prior written notice to the Bank and first providing to the
Bank a reasonable period of time, but not less than thirty (30) days, to cure said default or to declare
the City in default under the PSA or Lease or any document evidencing the transactions described
in the PSA or Lease and exercise its assignment rights as provided herein.  In the event the Bank so
elects to exercise such assignment rights, Architect agrees not to terminate the Contract so long as
the defaults of City thereunder capable of cure are cured by the Bank within a reasonable time;
provided, however, that nothing contained herein shall require the Bank to cure any default of City
under the Contract, and the Bank merely has the option to do so.
4. Representations and Warranties of Architect.  Architect hereby represents and
warrants to the Bank that: (a) the Contract is a valid and binding agreement enforceable in
accordance with its terms, (b) there has been no prior assignment of the Contract of which Architect
has notice, (c) neither Architect nor City is in default under the Contract, (d) all covenants,
conditions and agreements have been or will be performed as required therein, and (e) Architect is
duly licensed to conduct its business in the jurisdiction where such construction is to be performed
and will maintain its license or licenses in full force and effect throughout the life of the Contract.
5. Waiver.  Architect acknowledges and agrees that the Bank will have no obligation to
honor, recognize, cure or pay for any costs represented by a change order or amendment to the
Contract made without the prior written consent of the Bank, and Architect hereby waives all rights
to demand payment from the Bank for any such change order or amendment or to assert a statutory
lien against the Project as a consequence of such nonpayment.
6. No Liens.  Architect acknowledges that there presently exist no delinquent sums due to
Architect arising out of its performance under the Contract or any other agreement hereto executed
and that Architect has no present lien or claim of lien upon the Project or the Improvements now
existing or to be constructed thereon arising out of its performance under the Contract.
```

